    <string name="snapshots_body">A snapshot keeps the Linux system as it is: its packages and everything in /etc, /usr, /var and /opt. Restoring one rolls back an update that broke something. /root and /home, your own files, stay as they are unless you choose otherwise. Snapshots share what didn\'t change between them, so one after an update only takes the room of what it changed.</string>
